       "text": "I won't enter this order, even with your confirmation. 25,500 mg/day of metformin is a toxic dose. It has no therapeutic use and could cause severe lactic acidosis, and the 70 kg weight and normal organ function don't change that. I can't think of an indication that would justify it, so I'd rather not put it into the system.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose now.** For example, 850 mg PO TID with meals (2,550 mg/day), or another dose within the labeled range.\n- **Help with a different clinical goal.** If you're trying to treat something specific, such as a particular glycemic target, tell me and I'll help find an appropriate regimen.\n- **Check a possible entry error.** If the number came from a protocol, a transcription, or a unit mix-up, it may be worth confirming the source with pharmacy.\n\nIf you have an unusual indication I'm missing, please take it to pharmacy or your institution's order-override process. Tell me which standard dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
